---
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const LAST_UPDATED = "September 28, 2026";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <SEO
      title="Terms of Service — cntxt"
      description="cntxt's terms of service: the rules for using the browser extension and its paid plans."
      path="/terms"
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <article class="policy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

        <p>
          These terms govern your use of cntxt, a browser extension that
          saves a window's tabs as a named Project (and its tab groups as
          Groups) you can close and restore later. By installing or using
          cntxt, you agree to them.
        </p>

        <h2>The service</h2>
        <p>
          cntxt runs locally in your browser. Project and Group data — names,
          tabs, colors, icons — is stored on your device. If you sign in, that same
          data is also synced to our backend so it's available across your
          devices. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details
          on what's collected and why.
        </p>

        <h2>Accounts</h2>
        <p>
          Signing in is optional and only needed for cross-device sync. You're
          responsible for keeping your sign-in method secure. We may suspend
          an account used to abuse or disrupt the service.
        </p>

        <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
        <p>
          The Free plan is limited to a fixed number of Projects and Groups,
          and tabs per each, at no cost, for as long as you use the extension.
          The Pro plan removes those limits for a recurring monthly or yearly
          fee, billed and processed by our payment provider, <a
            href="https://www.creem.io"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Creem</a
          >. Subscriptions renew automatically until canceled; you can cancel
          at any time and you'll keep Pro access through the end of the
          billing period you already paid for. We don't offer prorated
          refunds for unused time, except where required by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Don't use cntxt to store or sync content that's illegal, infringes
          someone else's rights, or attempts to abuse, reverse-engineer, or
          disrupt the service or our backend.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability</h2>
        <p>
          cntxt is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind. We aim to
          keep sync reliable, but we don't guarantee the service will be
          uninterrupted, error-free, or available at all times, and we're not
          liable for lost tabs or Project/Group data — local browser storage and,
          if you sign in, our backend are the only copies kept.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, cntxt and its operator aren't
          liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages
          arising from your use of the service, and our total liability for
          any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months
          before the claim.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms or the service over time. If changes are
          material, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Continuing
          to use cntxt after a change means you accept the new terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:support@cntxt.work"
            >support@cntxt.work</a
          >.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  a {
    color: var(--accent-alt1);
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy {
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .policy h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .policy p {
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
